---
import '../styles/global.css';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<Header />

<main class="about-page">

  <!-- ===== HERO ===== -->

  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="about-hero-inner">

      <p class="about-label">About PZ Clean</p>

      <h1>
        Experience That Shapes Better Training
      </h1>

      <p class="about-hero-intro">
        PZ Clean Medical Training brings together operational medicine,
        clinical practice, and medical education to prepare people to
        respond when the situation is uncertain and the stakes are real.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ===== WHO WE ARE ===== -->

  <section class="about-intro">
    <div class="about-container about-intro-grid">

      <div class="about-intro-heading">
        <p class="about-label">Who We Are</p>

        <h2>
          Medical Training Grounded in Experience
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="about-intro-copy">

        <p class="about-lead">
          PZ Clean was built around a simple idea: medical training should
          prepare people to perform, not simply complete a course.
        </p>

        <p>
          Our instruction is informed by experience across military medicine,
          emergency and clinical care, austere environments, and medical
          education. That perspective shapes how we teach the fundamentals,
          develop scenarios, and prepare students to make decisions when
          real emergencies do not follow a script.
        </p>

        <p>
          Whether the audience is a healthcare professional, response team,
          business, outdoor organization, or community group, the objective
          remains the same: build practical capability and confidence.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ===== EXPERIENCE ===== -->

  <section class="about-experience">
    <div class="about-container">

      <div class="about-section-heading about-heading-light">
        <p>Built on Experience</p>
        <h2>From Operational Medicine to the Classroom</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="about-experience-grid">

        <article>
          <span></span>

          <h3>Operational Medicine</h3>

          <p>
            More than two decades of military service included extensive
            experience supporting complex operations, austere environments,
            medical teams, and high-consequence missions.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span></span>

          <h3>Clinical Practice</h3>

          <p>
            Years of clinical practice provide a foundation in practical
            patient care, medical decision-making, and the realities of
            managing illness and injury outside the classroom.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span></span>

          <h3>Medical Education</h3>

          <p>
            Experience teaching medical personnel, response teams, and
            community learners informs an approach centered on clear
            instruction, deliberate practice, and useful feedback.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span></span>

          <h3>Austere & Remote Environments</h3>

          <p>
            Training is shaped by experience in environments where resources
            may be limited, evacuation may be delayed, and good decisions
            matter as much as technical skill.
          </p>
        </article>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ===== WHY EXPERIENCE MATTERS ===== -->

  <section class="about-method">
    <div class="about-container about-method-grid">

      <div class="about-method-heading">

        <p class="about-label">Why It Matters</p>

        <h2>
          Experience is Useful Only if it Makes the Training Better
        </h2>

      </div>

      <div class="about-method-points">

        <article>
          <span></span>

          <div>
            <h3>Focus on What Matters</h3>

            <p>
              Students learn the core skills and decisions that have the
              greatest impact when time, information, or resources are limited.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span></span>

          <div>
            <h3>Make Training Relevant</h3>

            <p>
              Courses are connected to realistic environments, problems,
              and decisions rather than taught only as isolated skills.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span></span>

          <div>
            <h3>Build Confidence Through Practice</h3>

            <p>
              Students are given opportunities to apply what they learn,
              receive feedback, and develop confidence before the skill
              is needed for real.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ===== LEADERSHIP ===== -->

  <section class="about-founder">
    <div class="about-container">

      <div class="about-founder-card">

        <div class="about-founder-title">

          <p class="about-label">Leadership</p>

          <h2>Frank Brown</h2>

          <p class="about-founder-credentials">
            MPAS, DMSc, PA-C
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="about-founder-copy">

          <p>
            Frank Brown is a board-certified Physician Assistant, military
            veteran, and medical educator with more than two decades of
            experience spanning military and operational medicine, clinical
            practice, austere medical support, and medical training.
          </p>

          <p>
            His military career included service in specialized operational
            medical organizations and leadership of medical teams responsible
            for supporting complex missions in challenging environments.
            Following military retirement, he continues to practice clinically
            while developing and delivering medical education for professional,
            organizational, and community audiences.
          </p>

          <p>
            PZ Clean Medical Training was developed to bring those experiences
            together into practical education focused on strong fundamentals,
            sound judgment, and confident performance.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ===== CREDENTIALS ===== -->

  <section class="about-credentials">
    <div class="about-container">

      <div class="about-section-heading">
        <p>Professional Foundation</p>
        <h2>Clinical. Operational. Educational.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="about-credential-grid">

        <article>
          <span>20+</span>
          <h3>Years of Military Service</h3>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>PA-C</span>
          <h3>Board-Certified Physician Assistant</h3>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>DMSc</span>
          <h3>Doctor of Medical Science</h3>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>Global</span>
          <h3>Operational & Austere Experience</h3>
        </article>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ===== CTA ===== -->

  <section class="about-cta">

    <div class="about-cta-inner">

      <div>
        <p>Train With Purpose</p>

        <h2>
          Prepare Your Team to Respond.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="about-cta-actions">

        <a class="primary-button" href="/training">
          Explore Training
        </a>

        <a class="secondary-button" href="/contact">
          Contact PZ Clean
        </a>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>
</main>
